Q8. Explain the different types of CSS used for applying styles to an HTML document. Describe each type with a suitable example.

Answer:

There are three types of CSS.

1. Inline CSS

It is written directly inside an HTML tag.

Example:

<p style="color: red;">Hello</p>

2. Internal CSS

It is written inside the <style> tag in the HTML file.

Example:

<style>
p {
    color: blue;
}
</style>

3. External CSS

It is written in a separate CSS file and connected with the HTML file.

HTML:

<link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">

style.css:

p {
    color: green;
}

External CSS is useful when the same styles are needed on multiple webpages.


Q9. Differentiate between HTML, CSS, and JavaScript based on their role in developing a web page. Explain what each technology contributes to a website.

Answer:

HTML, CSS and JavaScript have different roles in a webpage.

HTML is used for the structure of the webpage. It creates things like headings, paragraphs, images and buttons.

CSS is used for the design of the webpage. It changes colors, fonts, sizes, spacing and layout.

JavaScript is used for making the webpage interactive. It can respond to clicks, change content and perform different actions.

In simple words:

HTML = Structure
CSS = Design
JavaScript = Interaction


